 strict unexpected passes and 8 characterizations passed, so the code was complete), added LLR-368 tags on refresh, attest and _AttestPlan, removed the 42 marks and the stand-in, re-stamped integrate.py down (1801 to 1793), wrote the RESYNC entry at the new base, and built C4 on disjoint files. Fixture census (decision 9 and D17): every [bars] declarer carries red_mark (conftest declare_review_bar and its callers, the BARS_RED_MARK and RED_MARK constants, test_integrate_station ATTEST_STACK_INI, test_integrate_attest's refusal table); the [product]-only declarations that reach the refresh gain BARS_RED_MARK (test_integrate_station STATION_STACK_INI and the station_repo users, test_id_landing _trunk, test_loop_provenance _station_repo, test_dispatch stub_harness_repo and census_repo, WI-1002's parked_beside_ready_repo inheriting it); the template-copying fixtures inherit it; test_red_mark_lane's lane-without-the-key case omits it on purpose. No red-mark test skips on this machine, so no skip disposition is owed. C3 and C4 commit as two attests, as the plan orders. The lane's round count starts at zero at its first review.\"\n+alternative = \"Discard the partial build and rebuild C3 from the plan.\"\n+reversal_cost = \"Low while uncommitted; the review rounds judge the result either way.\"\n+why_not_escalated = \"The handoff's direction (keep the work, discard only on a recorded finding) and the plan's commit table.\"\n+review = \"\"\n+\n+[decision.D-004]\n+decided = \"Round 1 (counted, at fed479a; files 001 and 002). REVIEW-B's MAJOR (with a tests root of `.`, the mark count read the whole tree, so the declaration in docs/stack.ini counted as marked and every refresh refused) is confirmed and fixed in one fix round: the one counter, red_mark.tree_counts, which all three counting reads use (attest's staged and reference trees, the refresh's staged tree), now counts only the files the review set reads as tests, through one predicate in kitlib/spine.py; a TC-422 test with `tests = .` failed on the pre-fix code (docs/stack.ini: 1 marked) and passes after. The other findings cost no round: REVIEW-B's coverage-bound MINOR (an added `reason=` argument counts 0) gets procedure text only, Intent step 2 saying the declared text is written verbatim with no added arguments; the spec's bound sentence sits inside the Done-when, so editing it would unbind the pass record, and it is a follow-up. REVIEW-A's three MINORs (SR-156's appended sentence against LLR-368's deleted-file exemption, LLR-368's plan-label coverage bound, TC-132's overclaimed method) and REVIEW-B's two row MINORs (the plan labels, LLR-368's write_blobs symbol) go to the checkpoint reconcile. REVIEW-B's MINOR on the missing landing-consequence entry is answered by D-005. Both coverage plans gate to exit 0 when run alone, each excluding the Done-when items by citing the accepted plan (the gate judges each plan file on its own, so the accepted plan beside a coverage plan fails on its own lines).\"\n+alternative = \"Leave out only the declaration file from the count.\"\n+reversal_cost = \"Low: one predicate.\"\n+why_not_escalated = \"A MAJOR costs a fix round under the cap; the fix stays inside the counting primitive the plan names.\"\n+review = \"\"\n+\n+[decision.D-005]\n+decided = \"The landing consequence (the Done-when's decisions-record item and plan decision 29): every lane cut before WI-996 lands refuses at `attest` until it rebases or refreshes onto the trunk that carries `[bars] red_mark`. On 2026-11-07 (git worktree list, and trunk's tracked claims under docs/work/active/, which hold only wi-996) that is the wi-902 worktree at bf96c4de7, whose claim trunk no longer tracks, and the branch codex/simplify-spine-resync at D:/ai-template-spine-resync, if either is ever attested; no other open claim exists. The fix round also moved the review set's test-file rule (the hidden-path check and the test-file suffix list) byte for byte out of gen_arch_map.py into kitlib/spine.py beside the declared test roots, so the counter and the tag reader call one predicate rather than a second copy; gen_arch_map.py sits outside the plan's file list, so the move is recorded here for the owner to confirm or overrule, and the RESYNC entry lists it among the files to overwrite.\"\n+alternative = \"Keep a second copy of the test-file rule in red_mark.py, or file a preparatory row for the move.\"\n+reversal_cost = \"Low: a byte-for-byte move back.\"\n+why_not_escalated = \"One module outside the named surface read the rule, and a copy would breach PROCESS.md section 3's consolidate-don't-duplicate rule; the reviewers judge it in round 2.\"\n+review = \"\"\ndiff --git a/docs/iteration/call_6e8d7b928a7c4b628e61795257756c29-20261107-010605.log b/docs/iteration/call_6e8d7b928a7c4b628e61795257756c29-20261107-010605.log\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 000000000..06daeee7f\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/iteration/call_6e8d7b928a7c4b628e61795257756c29-20261107-010605.log\n@@ -0,0 +1,99 @@\n+# agent session log — written by scripts/agent_common.py\n+# session: call_6e8d7b928a7c4b628e61795257756c29\n+# date: 2026-11-07 01:06\n+# train:\n+# base:\n+# phase: CRITIQUE\n+# wi:\n+# model: gpt-6.1-sol\n+# guardrails:\n+# outcome: COMPLETED\n+# commits:\n+# review-scope:\n+# bar-red:\n+# bar-summary:\n+# tokens:\n+# cost-usd:\n+# wall-secs: 122\n+# api-secs:\n+# turns:\n+# ttft-secs:\n+# cache-read:\n+# cache-create:\n+# effort:\n+# fast:\n+# prompt-chars:\n+# prompt-template:\n+# prompt-sha:\n+# timeout:\n+# heterogeneity:\n+# exit-code: 0\n+# session-id: 01a1b4d2-50b1-7041-8052-19bdd54b93a6\n+# context-used: 82992\n+# context-window: 475000\n+# context-pct: 17\n+# session-gen:\n+# reset-reason:\n+# session-mode: fresh\n+# keep-scope:\n+# compacted:\n+# compaction-source:\n+# invocation-id: 6e8d7b928a7c4b628e61795257756c29\n+# attempt-id:\n+# source-event: coordinator\n+# role: CRITIQUE\n+# provider: OPENAI\n+# tier: strong\n+# roster-row: OPENAI-SOL\n+# started-at: 2026-11-07T07